-- title:
--   Chains with boundary vanishing mod Γ₀(N) have lattice periods
-- statement:
--   Let $N$ be a positive natural number and let $Z$ be a finitely supported function from $\mathbb{H}\times\mathbb{H}$ to $\mathbb{Z}$, to be thought of as an integral chain $\sum_e Z(e)\,[e_1\to e_2]$ of oriented straight segments in the upper half plane. Assume that the boundary of $Z$ vanishes orbitwise: for every $\tau\in\mathbb{H}$, the sum over the support of $Z$ of the quantities $m\cdot\bigl(\mathbb{1}[\exists\,\gamma\in\Gamma_0(N),\ \gamma\cdot e_2=\tau]-\mathbb{1}[\exists\,\gamma\in\Gamma_0(N),\ \gamma\cdot e_1=\tau]\bigr)$, with $m=Z(e)$ and the action that of $\mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb{Z})$ on $\mathbb{H}$ by Möbius transformations, equals $0$. The conclusion is that the element $\sum_e Z(e)\cdot \mathrm{periodAlong}\,N\,e_1\,e_2$ of the $\mathbb{C}$-dual of the space of weight-$2$ cusp forms for $\Gamma_0(N)$ belongs to [`ModularCurve.periodLattice N`](def/ModularCurve_PeriodLattice.html#L102). Here $\mathrm{periodAlong}\,N\,\tau_0\,\tau_1$ is the linear functional $f\mapsto\int_0^1 f(\mathrm{segmentPath}\,\tau_0\,\tau_1\,t)\,(\tau_1-\tau_0)\,dt$, the integral of $f\,d\tau$ along the straight segment from $\tau_0$ to $\tau_1$, and `periodLattice N` is the $\mathbb{Z}$-span of the functionals $\mathrm{periodAlong}\,N\,i\,(\gamma\cdot i)$ for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(N)$.
--
--   This is the well-definedness statement underlying the Abel–Jacobi map on the modular curve $X_0(N)$ in the form needed here: the total period of an integral chain of geodesic-free straight segments depends only on its boundary modulo $\Gamma_0(N)$, so a chain that is closed in the quotient has period in the lattice generated by the periods $\int_i^{\gamma i}f\,d\tau$. The proof invokes the existence of an equivariant primitive ([`ModularCurve.exists_hasEquivariantPrimitive`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_hasEquivariantPrimitive)) for each weight-$2$ cusp form, and the result feeds into [`ModularCurve.periodAlong_add_petersson_mem_periodLattice_of_multiplier_eq_exp`](thm.html#ModularCurve.periodAlong_add_petersson_mem_periodLattice_of_multiplier_eq_exp).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_sum_periodAlong_mem_periodLattice_of_boundary_eq_zero.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_PeriodLattice

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

open UpperHalfPlane
open scoped MatrixGroups

open Classical in

theorem ModularCurve.sum_periodAlong_mem_periodLattice_of_boundary_eq_zero
    {N : ℕ} [NeZero N] (Z : (ℍ × ℍ) →₀ ℤ)
    (hZ : ∀ τ : ℍ,
      Z.sum (fun e m =>
        (if ∃ γ : CongruenceSubgroup.Gamma0 N, (γ : SL(2, ℤ)) • e.2 = τ then m else 0) -
        (if ∃ γ : CongruenceSubgroup.Gamma0 N, (γ : SL(2, ℤ)) • e.1 = τ then m else 0)) = 0) :
    (Z.sum fun e m => m • ModularCurve.periodAlong N e.1 e.2) ∈
      ModularCurve.periodLattice N := by sorry
